     "text": "Certainly! Based on the guidelines and updates provided by Daniel, I've created a **Nearest Neighbors** model class that adheres to the latest coding standards and conventions discussed in the mentorship sessions. The class follows the naming conventions and best practices that have been emphasized, including consistent naming of variables and methods, and the use of clear, readable code.\n\nHere is the implementation:\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nclass NearestNeighbors:\n    \"\"\"\n    A simple implementation of the k-Nearest Neighbors algorithm.\n    This class is designed to be used for classification tasks.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, n_neighbors=5):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initialize the Nearest Neighbors model.\n\n        Parameters:\n        n_neighbors (int): Number of neighbors to consider for classification.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.n_neighbors = n_neighbors\n        self._X = None  # Training data\n        self._y = None  # Target labels\n\n    def fit(self, X, y):\n        \"\"\"\n        Train the model using the provided training data and labels.\n\n        Parameters:\n        X (array-like): Training data of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n        y (array-like): Target labels of shape (n_samples,)\n        \"\"\"\n        self._X = np.array(X)\n        self._y = np.array(y)\n\n    def _distance(self, x1, x2):\n        \"\"\"\n        Compute the Euclidean distance between two samples.\n\n        Parameters:\n        x1 (array-like): First sample\n        x2 (array-like): Second sample\n\n        Returns:\n        float: Euclidean distance between x1 and x2\n        \"\"\"\n        return np.linalg.norm(x1 - x2)\n\n    def _get_neighbors(self, X, y, sample_index):\n        \"\"\"\n        Find the indices of the nearest neighbors for a given sample.\n\n        Parameters:\n        X (array-like): Training data\n        y (array-like): Target labels\n        sample_index (int): Index of the sample in X to find neighbors for\n\n        Returns:\n        list: Indices of the nearest neighbors\n        \"\"\"\n        distances = [self._distance(X[sample_index], X[i]) for i in range(len(X))]\n        sorted_indices = np.argsort(distances)\n        return sorted_indices[:self.n_neighbors]\n\n    def predict(self, X):\n        \"\"\"\n        Predict the class labels for the provided test samples.\n\n        Parameters:\n        X (array-like): Test samples of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n\n       ",
